course: dictionary
lesson: 10660
title: Unknowing and unaware
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Unknowing means not knowing, or not aware of what is happening, often something important. The prefix un- means not, and know is in the middle, so unknowing is "not knowing." «A scientist showed that Hans was watching tiny, unknowing movements of the people around him.»
explain: The people were making tiny movements without realising it. They relaxed when Hans reached the right number, and he stopped. They were unknowing: they did not know their small movements were giving him a signal.
explain: Stories use this word too. An unknowing victim does not know danger is coming, and an unknowing helper does something without realising what it is part of. Notice how the word tells you what the character does not know.
fact: Unknowing means not aware of something, often something important.
fact: The word is built from un- (not) and knowing: not knowing.
fact: An unknowing helper does something without realising what it is part of.
fact: «Unknowingly» is the adverb, and it tells you how someone does something.
fact: When a reader knows something a character does not, this is called dramatic irony.
exercise: «A scientist showed that Hans was watching tiny, unknowing movements of the people around him.» What does unknowing mean here? | Known to everyone | *Not aware of what is happening | Happy and smiling | Very loud
exercise: In unknowing, the prefix un- means what? | Under | Again | *Not | Before
exercise: What is an unknowing helper? | Someone who refuses to help | *Someone who helps without realising what it is part of | Someone who is very tired | Someone who helps on purpose, with a clear plan
test: «She unknowingly walked past the danger.» What does unknowingly tell you? | She walked past in a hurry to catch a bus | She walked past loudly and angrily | She walked past the danger on purpose | *She did not know she was passing danger
test: What is an unknowing victim in a story? | A brave hero who fights the villain | Someone who knows the danger and runs away | *Someone who does not know danger is coming | A teacher who explains the plan
exam: Jayden reads a mystery where the reader knows the thief is hiding, but the detective does not. Which word best describes the detective? | Famous | Cheerful | Hungry | *Unknowing
